Before editing, testing, committing, pushing, opening a PR, merging or deploying,
read and obey `/AI_WORK_POLICY.md`.

The repository uses LOCAL-FIRST development.

Local commits are checkpoints.
GitHub pushes are expensive release-verification events.

Do not push intermediate work.

A local checkpoint is `git commit`, not `git push`.
Remote sync requires `TRADEAI_REMOTE_PUSH_AUTHORIZED=1` plus operator intent.

Runtime notes: `AGENTS.md`. Do not duplicate the policy here.
